hey everyone its Johanna here when it  comes to staying healthy and fit  exercising only contributes 20% and your  food in fact contributes 80% to your  success hence picking the right food  when you do your grocery shopping is  crucial to maintaining a healthy weight  so if you are new to eating a healthy  and well-balanced diet or if you like to  clean up your food cupboard here are  several food categories that you need to  have in your grocery list before you do  your grocery shopping it is important to  first roughly plan your meals out for  the week if you go without knowing what  you want and just buy whatever that  seems to appeal to you chances are you  will end up with more junk foods than  wholesome food second do not ever shop  when you are hungry everything will seem  more appealing and chances are you will  end up with more foods that you don't  need especially junk foods so here's a  basic healthy grocery shopping guide you  can start with the first food category  that you need is complex cups or starchy  cups complex Cup is essential as part of  your meals to stabilize blood sugar  level and to keep your energy level up  this should make a quarter of your meal  some of the examples include quinoa  oatmeal brown rice couscous whole wheat  pasta  sweet potato high-fiber cereal whole  grain bread and more so ask yourself  what are you having for breakfast are  you having oatmeal whole grain bread or  cereals what about lunch and dinner are  you having brown rice bread quinoa or  pasta chances are you can buy a huge  selection of dried complex carbs because  they will last and store for a long time  second food category your protein  consuming protein in your meals will  help to keep you satisfied for much  longer and to reduce cravings again this  should make a quarter of your meals  choose three to four different varieties  some of my favorite proteins include  salmon chicken eggs and canned beans  other examples include any other fish  seafood red meat which should be  consumed occasionally as they are higher  in saturated fat tofu tempeh canned tuna  protein bars or protein powder and more  so if you are a busy person and have  very the time to prep meals I would  suggest to buy more easy to go protein  such as canned tuna canned beans and  protein bar this way when you are tight  on time you will still be able to pack  in your protein and to curb hunger third  food category vegetables buy them in  abundance this should make out the  largest part of your grocery shopping  and also your meals they are extremely  low in calories high in fiber  hence help to curb hunger and it is hard  to over eat them buy as many varieties  as you want and have at least two green  leafy vegetables some of my favorite  vegetables which you have seen a lot in  my recipes include broccoli carrots  spinach lettuce canned tomatoes onions  and garlic to enhance the flavors I tend  to buy more frozen vegetables because  they last longer and they are much  cheaper in price as well shop according  to your budget buy seasonal fruits or  vegetables and buy them in box if you  can't finish them you can always chop  and freeze them up so nothing will ever  go to waste  this leads onto my next food category  fruits for fruits I would encourage you  to buy either fresh fruits or frozen  fruits try to avoid canned fruits as  most of them are soaked in syrup hence  high amount of added sugar you can buy  frozen fruits or freeze fresh fruits to  make healthy and delicious smoothies  another tip is to always keep fresh  fruit at home in your bag or at work so  when you need a quick sugar boost you  will have a fruit to turn to food  category number five is your snacks yes  they are extremely important and should  be part of your grocery list your snacks  can either be the key to  achieve your goal or it can be the  culprit to your weight gain whatever  snacks you buy you will eat them so  choose your snacks wisely some of the  healthy snacks to go for include nuts or  seeds dried fruits such as apricot or  goji berries fresh fruits whole grain  crackers you get vegetables popcorn and  more snacks you shoot by occasionally or  avoid storing at home especially if you  know you have the tendency to indulge a  little too far include chips chocolate  bars especially those loaded with sugar  sweets cakes biscuits pastries ice cream  basically any processed food which are  high in calories and loaded with fat and  sugar my advice is not to buy them as  part of your weekly grocery shopping  personally if I crave for a naughty food  I would then go out and buy one this  takes more effort and reduces the chance  of me indulging in them on a regular  basis the next food category is what I  call flavors just think about how do you  intend to cook and add flavors into your  food because the last thing you want is  to eat a plain piece of chicken or fish  yet at the same time we do not want to  add lots of high-calorie sauce just to  flavor our chicken which makes it from  being a really healthy meal to an  unhealthy meal the best way to add  flavors into your cooking without adding  extra calories sodium or fat is to use  spices I love my spices I would say at  least choose 2 to 3 different varieties  what I have here are ground cumin chili  powder dried mixed herbs and dried  parsley so use these hubs to dry rub it  into your chicken breast then roast it  grill it or sear it healthy food will  never be boring or tasteless again other  essential flavors to have include olive  oil 1 calorie spray especially if you do  a lot of baking natural sweeteners such  as honey stevia or maple syrup lemon and  peanut butter or fruit gel for your  morning toast and oatmeal and the final  food  degree dreams we should be drinking at  least 2.5 to 3 litres of water a day and  do very mind that this include other  fluids as well drinking water on its own  can be plain and boring to most people  so do consider adding other healthy  drinks to meet your daily fluid  requirements this includes green tea or  any other tea and coffee do drink them  in moderation especially if you are  sensitive to caffeine other drinks you  can include our lemon juice apple cider  vinegar hot chocolate sir look or any  other milk and more again consume them  in for duration as they can add to your  daily calorie intake drinks you should  not store at home are fruit juices as  they tend to have a lot of added sugar  soda drinks energy drinks and alcohol if  you really have to consume them in  absolute minimal so the next time you  plan to do your grocery shopping follow  these three steps first has this 7 food  category list with you second roughly  plan your meals for the week even better  not plan them in detail but write a  grocery list and stick by it  grocery shopping should be exciting  because you are buying foods to feed  your body so nourish your body with the  best foods because you deserve it on the  best for new Fitness food and  motivational videos please like share  and subscribe to my You Tube channel and  website do you follow me on Facebook  Instagram and Twitter to stay connected  with me thanks guys
 

